Subject: [PATCH 11/15] fix: code-review findings on the last four pushes

Four real findings, one already resolved by the lint pass:

- The "No unenforced guardrail" principle had no corresponding check
  in steward's numbered list, unlike "No redundant guardrails" ->
  check 7. Added check 11, and the same check to lint's checklist
  since lint mirrors steward's checks as a full-repo sweep.
- bootstrap's role-list-compiling step never said to give the two
  files base frontmatter, unlike every other stub-writing step in the
  same file. Added it.
- The same step gave no tiebreaker for roles whose track is genuinely
  ambiguous (compliance, quality, process-documentation). Added a
  default-to-process rule with the reasoning.
- docs/plans/product-process-track-and-domain-agnostic-scope.md's
  step 2 "done when" criterion quoted roadmap's paragraph verbatim,
  but later work (0013/0014) trimmed and extended it since. Noted the
  criterion is stale rather than leaving a future reader to wonder why
  a grep for the exact quote fails.

(The fifth finding -- three new guardrails shipped without their own
required governed-by/grounded-in/derivation-note fields -- was already
fixed by the lint pass in 1656b4f, which predates this commit.)
